  <h1>AI, Alignment as Standpoint, and Exact Intelligence</h1>
  <p class="lead">Contemporary AI alignment attempts to install behavioral rules into opaque statistical weights after training. Hyperactivity derives intelligence and safety from one mathematical primitive: partial observation fixes a <em>fiber</em> of compatible worlds, warrant requires a construction across the entire fiber, and alignment is a local standpoint relation verified on the participant's own device — never a corporate leash trained into a model.</p>

